// Where the Xcode build gets the PostHog project token. Tracked, and holding
// no token: the real one goes in Analytics.local.xcconfig beside this file,
// which .gitignore names for the same reason it names .env.
//
// This file has to exist. XcodeGen validates every path under `configFiles`
// and refuses to generate the project when one is missing, so ignoring this
// file instead of the local one would stop a fresh clone, and the release
// workflow with it, before the first build.
//
// The empty default is what a clone without a local file gets. The Info.plist
// then carries an empty SSPostHogProjectToken, PostHogClient reads that as
// missing, and the app measures nothing rather than refusing to start.
//
// No URL belongs in an xcconfig. // starts a comment here, so
// https://us.i.posthog.com would be cut at the scheme. POSTHOG_HOST is public
// and lives in project.yml, where nothing eats the slashes.
POSTHOG_PROJECT_TOKEN =

// Last, so the local value wins over the empty default above. The ? is what
// makes the file optional: a plain #include of a missing file fails the build.
#include? "Analytics.local.xcconfig"
